SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine’s Annual Hire-A-Vet Campaign
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nYou know\, one of the great privileges of serving as your Governor 
 is working with so many veterans to make sure they have all the opportunit
 ies that they deserve in our state. Our state is proud that we have one of
  the highest number of veterans per capita of any state in the country. An
 d we're here to serve them.\nI am proud to have the benefit of a number of
  veterans in my Administration\, including members of the Cabinet like Com
 missioner Randy Liberty\, Commissioner Mike Sauschuck\, Commissioner and A
 djutant General Diane Dunn\, as well as a wonderful group of Aide de Camp 
 who advised me and my Administration on issues relating to veterans.\nI al
 so come from a proud military family. Two uncles who fought in the Pacific
  in World War II. My brother who served three tours of duty in Vietnam\, a
 nd my father who served in the Pacific during World War II at the Battle o
 f Leyte Gulf. So I know that when our friends and family members come home
  from serving on the front lines\, they deserve every opportunity to find 
 rewarding careers in the civil sector that utilize their extensive skills\
 , diverse experiences\, and their unique training.\nMaine's Hire-A-Vet Cam
 paign\nis a key part of expanding those opportunities. The campaign had am
 bitious goals last year: 100 days\, 100 employers\, and 100 veterans hired
 . And thanks to everyone’s hard work\, we achieved those goals\, and we 
 place veterans in good-paying jobs in every county in Maine. The employers
  hiring the most veterans included the State of Maine itself\, Bonney Staf
 fing\, Northern Light Health\, and Bath Iron Works.\nSince its inception i
 n 2015\, the Hire-A-Vet Campaign has connected more than 2\,000 employers 
 with over 2\,200 veterans hired. That's incredible.\nAnd to all the busine
 sses who helped make that happen\, I say thank you. You folks hired Maine 
 veterans because you recognized what we all know to be true. Veterans know
  what it means to work as a team and to leave\nhttp://www.maine.gov/govern
 or/mills/news/radio_address/maines-annual-hire-vet-campaign-2026-08-28
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/maines-annual-h
 ire-vet-campaign-2026-08-28
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
