 its Manual is available on-line at the\nSecretary of State’s website\n.\
 nBelow\, please find a MaineCare Notice of Agency Rulemaking Proposal. You
  can access the complete rule at\nhttp://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/rules/inde
 x.shtml.\n________________________________________________________________
 ____________\nNotice of Agency Rulemaking Proposal\nAgency:\nDepartment of
  Health and Human Services\, Office of MaineCare Services\, Division of Po
 licy\nChapter Number and Rule Title:\n10-144 C.M.R. Ch. 101\, MaineCare Be
 nefits Manual (MBM) Ch. II\, Sec. 20\, Home and Community Based Services f
 or Adults with Other Related Conditions\nType of Rule:\nRoutine Technical\
 nBrief Summary:\nThis Section 20 rule regulates home and community-based s
 ervices (HCBS) that are authorized by a federal Medicaid Section 1915(c) H
 CBS waiver that meets federal standards. MBM Ch. II\, Sec. 20 authorizes M
 aineCare HCBS waiver services for adults with conditions other than autism
  spectrum disorder that are related to but distinguishable from intellectu
 al disabilities. Through this rulemaking the Department proposes to: align
  similar processes\, new services\, service descriptions\, definitions\, a
 nd provider requirements with Maine’s four other Section 1915(c) waivers
 \; make\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/maine
 care-notice-agency-rule-making-proposal-mainecare-benefits-manual-chapter-
 ii-11
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 notice-agency-rule-making-proposal-mainecare-benefits-manual-chapter-ii-11
